window.SIM4 = {"design":"ii0.11_flat_uniform_b1_sfree","steps":[{"id":"1","n":1,"title":"The network","map":"plain","body":"890 pipes and 328 manholes, with new homes coming by 2041. The question is what data shows growth using up these pipes, and where to collect it."},{"id":"2","n":2,"title":"A design wet day, today","map":"base","legend":["was"],"body":"Before any new homes, the model has 7 manholes surcharged: water above the pipe top, the warning sign before an overflow. None spill. On a much wetter day it has 107, so wet weather alone already matters."},{"id":"3","n":3,"title":"Add the 2041 homes","map":"growth","slider":true,"legend":["was","rise","tip"],"body":"Each region is built out on its own. R1, R3, R4, R7 and R9 rise 10 mm or more; R2, R5, R6 and R8 do not. At full build-out, no manhole newly surcharges and none spills."},{"id":"4","n":4,"title":"Decide where to look","map":"triage","legend":["monitor","watch","leave"],"body":"Monitor R3 and R7: likely to reach the pipe limit by 2041. Watch R1, R4 and R9: could go either way. Leave R2, R5, R6 and R8: room left. Not monitoring is a valid answer, if a design wet day is the right test."},{"id":"5a","n":5,"title":"Place sensors, if the design day is right","map":"sensors","k":1,"legend":["sensor","monitor","watch"],"body":"1 sensor sees all 16 growth runs in those regions on a design wet day. In other weather it falls short: 53% on average across 7 wet cases. Click a sensor to see why it is there."},{"id":"5b","n":5,"title":"Place sensors, if the weather is unknown","map":"sensors","k":5,"legend":["sensor","monitor","watch"],"body":"The same 1 plus 4 more. Across 7 wet cases they see 94% of growth runs on average and 81% in the worst case, and warn of all 11 overloads. On weather they were not chosen for: 77%."},{"id":"6","n":6,"title":"Cost, and doing it again","map":"sensors","k":5,"legend":["sensor"],"body":"$25k or $125k, at assumed prices. Real records of a normal day could confirm the design day and save up to 4 sensors, about $100k. A new suburb needs its own model runs: the method repeats, this sensor list does not."}],"popups":{"1":[{"name":"MH4450531","n":1,"listens":"R1, R3, R4, R7 and R9, on a design wet day","reacts":"14 new homes in R3 (+12.4 mm)","lost":"Design wet falls from 100% to 0% of growth runs","note":""}],"5":[{"name":"MH4450531","n":1,"listens":"R1, R3, R4, R7 and R9, on a design wet day","reacts":"14 new homes in R3 (+12.4 mm)","lost":"Worst case falls from 81% to 62%, average from 94% to 85%","note":""},{"name":"MH4448345","n":2,"listens":"In wetter weather only: R1 in 5 of 7 wet cases, R4 in 5 of 7 wet cases","reacts":"Stays under 10 mm on a design wet day, even with all 2041 homes","lost":"Worst case falls from 81% to 38%, average from 94% to 79%","note":""},{"name":"MH4450922","n":3,"listens":"R1, R3, R4, R7 and R9, on a design wet day","reacts":"27 new homes in R1 (+13.3 mm)","lost":"Worst case falls from 81% to 0%, average from 94% to 80%","note":"It is the only sensor here that sees a design wet day where older pipes leak more (age-weighted). The model has this manhole surcharged before any growth. Worth a site check."},{"name":"MH4452994","n":4,"listens":"In wetter weather only: R9 in 4 of 7 wet cases, R3 in 2 of 7 wet cases","reacts":"Stays under 10 mm on a design wet day, even with all 2041 homes","lost":"Worst case falls from 81% to 56%, average from 94% to 88%","note":"It sits in R2, which needs no sensor of its own. It is here for flow passing through."},{"name":"MH4428268","n":5,"listens":"In wetter weather only: R1 in 1 of 7 wet cases, R4 in 1 of 7 wet cases","reacts":"Stays under 10 mm on a design wet day, even with all 2041 homes","lost":"Worst case falls from 81% to 69%, average from 94% to 92%","note":""}]},"triage":{"R1":"watch","R2":"leave","R3":"monitor","R4":"watch","R5":"leave","R6":"leave","R7":"monitor","R8":"leave","R9":"watch"},"ladder":{"1":["MH4450531"],"5":["MH4450531","MH4448345","MH4450922","MH4452994","MH4428268"]},"expert":"<h2>Which regions</h2>\n<p>Design wet, pipe limit 0.7 of bore (assumed). Runs out means monitor, uncertain means watch, room left means leave. Bands by case: O runs out, U uncertain, R room left, A already over before growth. Regions: 8 holding near-equal numbers of existing homes, cut by the spatial bisection of Kim et al. (2022), plus R9, the Walkerville Terrace corridor, which overlaps them.</p>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Action</th><th>Band</th><th>2041 homes</th><th>Homes to limit, 10th to 90th</th><th>Band in the 7 wet cases</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>R1</td><td>Watch</td><td>uncertain</td><td>54</td><td>12 to 78</td><td>U O O U O A A</td></tr><tr><td>R2</td><td>Leave</td><td>room left</td><td>49</td><td>53 to beyond the top step</td><td>R U A R R U U</td></tr><tr><td>R3</td><td>Monitor</td><td>runs out</td><td>54</td><td>2 to 59</td><td>O O A R O A A</td></tr><tr><td>R4</td><td>Watch</td><td>uncertain</td><td>54</td><td>15 to 79</td><td>U A A U O A U</td></tr><tr><td>R5</td><td>Leave</td><td>room left</td><td>40</td><td>not reached</td><td>R R R R R R R</td></tr><tr><td>R6</td><td>Leave</td><td>room left</td><td>60</td><td>not reached</td><td>R R A R R R R</td></tr><tr><td>R7</td><td>Monitor</td><td>runs out</td><td>55</td><td>6 to 71</td><td>O A A R O A A</td></tr><tr><td>R8</td><td>Leave</td><td>room left</td><td>71</td><td>not reached</td><td>R A A R R A A</td></tr><tr><td>R9</td><td>Watch</td><td>uncertain</td><td>485</td><td>90 to 1271</td><td>U A A U U A A</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>The ladder</h2>\n<p>Each row adds one sensor to the row above. Target regions, build-out up to 100%, 7 wet cases, 10 mm rule unless stated. At least 96 five-sensor sets tie for best with the Design wet set, so read this as one good choice, not the only one.</p>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Sensors</th><th>Added</th><th>Worst / average</th><th>Design wet</th><th>25 mm rule</th><th>Warned</th><th>Exact solver, not nested</th><th>Assumed cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>MH4450531</td><td>0% / 53%</td><td>100%</td><td>0% / 21%</td><td>8 of 11</td><td>12% / 42%</td><td>$25k</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>MH4448345</td><td>0% / 72%</td><td>100%</td><td>0% / 34%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>43% / 62%</td><td>$50k</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>MH4450922</td><td>44% / 86%</td><td>100%</td><td>19% / 39%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>56% / 85%</td><td>$75k</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>MH4452994</td><td>69% / 92%</td><td>100%</td><td>36% / 44%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>81% / 91%</td><td>$100k</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>MH4428268</td><td>81% / 94%</td><td>100%</td><td>36% / 45%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>88% / 94%</td><td>$125k</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>MH4448474</td><td>88% / 96%</td><td>100%</td><td>36% / 50%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>94% / 96%</td><td>$150k</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>MH4428920</td><td>94% / 97%</td><td>100%</td><td>36% / 50%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>94% / 97%</td><td>$175k</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>MH4449704</td><td>94% / 98%</td><td>100%</td><td>36% / 52%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>94% / 98%</td><td>$200k</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Stand-ins for the five</h2>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>Worst / average without it</th><th>Warned without it</th><th>Stand-ins with the same score</th><th>Nearest</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MH4450531</td><td>62% / 85%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>4</td><td>MH4450391, MH4450137, MH4449796</td></tr><tr><td>MH4448345</td><td>38% / 79%</td><td>9 of 11</td><td>0</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td>MH4450922</td><td>0% / 80%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>3</td><td>MH4451207, MH4451871, MH4452011</td></tr><tr><td>MH4452994</td><td>56% / 88%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>23</td><td>MH4453489, MH4453579, MH4453970</td></tr><tr><td>MH4428268</td><td>69% / 92%</td><td>11 of 11</td><td>0</td><td>none</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>How it holds up</h2>\n<p>Chosen without the weather case or region tested, always exactly the stated number of sensors. Random is 5,000 draws on the same runs. On an unseen region, 5 sensors see 76% against 55% for random manholes that respond at all: the picks still beat random manholes on a region they were not chosen for. Age-weighted Design wet cannot be predicted from the other weather: chosen without it, 8 sensors see 0% of it. R9 shares its manholes with the regions it crosses, so holding it out does not hide it, and the unseen-region figure is a little generous.</p>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Sensors</th><th>Unseen weather</th><th>Warned</th><th>Unseen region</th><th>Warned</th><th>Random responsive, average</th><th>Warned</th><th>Random any, average</th><th>Warned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>55%</td><td>8 of 11</td><td>50%</td><td>8 of 11</td><td>22%</td><td>3.5</td><td>9%</td><td>1.5</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>71%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>60%</td><td>8 of 11</td><td>34%</td><td>5.6</td><td>17%</td><td>2.9</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>71%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>66%</td><td>8 of 11</td><td>43%</td><td>6.9</td><td>24%</td><td>3.9</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>49%</td><td>7.8</td><td>28%</td><td>4.6</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>77%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>55%</td><td>8.3</td><td>33%</td><td>5.4</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>78%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>58%</td><td>8.7</td><td>38%</td><td>6.1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>78%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>62%</td><td>9.0</td><td>41%</td><td>6.5</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>79%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>76%</td><td>10 of 11</td><td>65%</td><td>9.2</td><td>44%</td><td>7.0</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Fewest sensors by weather covered</h2>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Weather to cover</th><th>80%</th><th>90%</th><th>100%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Design wet only</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Design wet + Beyond design</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Design wet family (3)</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>All 7 wet cases</td><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Where the model really overloads by 100%</h2>\n<p>Manholes that newly surcharge or spill, any wet case. A surcharge is a warning sign, not an overflow: 50 rows of 315 show a new surcharge and 1 a new spill.</p>\n<table class=\"\"><thead><tr><th>Manhole</th><th>Runs</th><th>Spilling</th><th>Weather cases</th><th>Growth in</th><th>Sits in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MH4501866</td><td>20</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R2, R5, R6, R8, R9</td><td>R5</td></tr><tr><td>MH4448345</td><td>15</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R1, R3, R4, R7, R9</td><td>R4</td></tr><tr><td>MH4453850</td><td>5</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>R9</td><td>R2</td></tr><tr><td>MH4429268</td><td>4</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R3, R9</td><td>R7</td></tr><tr><td>MH4449977</td><td>4</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R1, R4, R9</td><td>R4</td></tr><tr><td>MH4429527</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R3, R9</td><td>R3</td></tr><tr><td>MH4449011</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R1, R4, R9</td><td>R7</td></tr><tr><td>MH4451945</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R2</td><td>R2</td></tr><tr><td>MH4501851</td><td>3</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R9</td><td>R5</td></tr><tr><td>MH4454376</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R9</td><td>R6, R9</td></tr><tr><td>MH4428268</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R1</td><td>R1</td></tr><tr><td>MH4451886</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>R9</td><td>R7, R9</td></tr><tr><td>MH4452809</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R9</td><td>R7</td></tr><tr><td>MH4453788</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>R9</td><td>R2</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>What limits this</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No calibration: every figure is a model result, a guide to where to look first. No field data was available.</li>\n<li>The 10 mm and 25 mm rules, the pipe limit, the bands and both prices are assumed.</li>\n<li>One simulated run moves a weather case's score by 5 to 7 points. Read smaller differences as noise.</li>\n<li>Leave depends on Design wet. R5 alone keeps room in all 7 wet cases.</li>\n<li>Homes are per region, each built out on its own. R9's 2041 figure is the whole 485-home anchor by design, not a share of a total.</li>\n<li>Sensors never fail here. Long-term sensor losses are not modelled.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What a new suburb must supply (draft)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Pipes and manholes: positions, inverts, diameters, lids.</li>\n<li>Its outlet and exit pipes, and how water leaves the modelled area.</li>\n<li>Homes now and projected, and how the suburb is divided into regions.</li>\n<li>Where homes connect, and pump stations with their rates.</li>\n<li>The weather cases and inflow rates to test.</li>\n<li>The pipe limit, the rise rule and sensor prices, ideally the utility's own.</li>\n<li>For a greenfield estate, where it may join: here, a main of 225 mm or more.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Greenfield</h2>\n<p>Not fully analysed. Four of its eight weather cases are not settled runs, and it has no warning or room analysis. It stays out of the story. Its coverage curve is in the earlier tool below.</p>\n<p>Where a new estate could join: at a manhole whose widest outgoing pipe is 225 mm or more, 91 of the 328 candidate manholes here. An estate lays its own pipes and joins a trunk main, not a street sewer. The rule is a team member's proposal. It is a team assumption, not a utility standard, and whether that main has room for a given estate is a separate check.</p>\n<h2>Earlier tool</h2>\n<p><a href=\"../simulation35/index.html\">Sim 3.5</a> keeps every control and table from the 6 November demo. Its five-sensor sets predate this ladder, it uses the hand-picked regions, and it covers all 8 regions and the stress steps, so its figures differ.</p>\n<p>The map's wheel zoom is from the team's buildings demo.</p>\n","stepCount":6};
